Payroll Policy Version: 1.0 Department: Human Resources & Payroll Effective Date: January 1, 2026 1. Purpose This payroll policy outlines the procedures governing employee compensation, salary payments, statutory deductions, bonuses, and payroll administration. The objective is to ensure: • Timely salary processing • Accurate payroll calculations • Compliance with statutory regulations • Transparent employee communication 2. Scope This policy applies to: • Permanent employees • Probationary employees • Contract employees (unless otherwise specified in employment agreements) 3. Payroll Cycle Monthly Payroll Processing Payroll is processed monthly. Salary Credit Date Salaries are credited on the last working day of each month. If the salary credit date falls on a public holiday or weekend, salary will be credited on the preceding working day. Payroll Cut-off Date The payroll cut-off date is the 25th of every month. ABC Public Changes submitted after the cut-off date may be reflected in the following month's payroll cycle. 4. Salary Structure Employee compensation may contain the following components: Earnings Basic Salary • Forms the foundation of the employee's compensation. • Usually constitutes 40% to 50% of fixed pay. House Rent Allowance (HRA) • Provided to employees to support housing expenses. • Calculated according to payroll guidelines. Special Allowance • Balancing component of fixed compensation. • Taxed according to applicable laws. Variable Pay • Performance-based compensation. • Paid based on achievement of business and individual objectives. Annual Bonus • Paid once annually based on company performance and employee ratings. 5. Statutory Deductions Provident Fund (PF) Employee contribution: 12% of Basic Salary Employer contribution: 12% of Basic Salary PF contributions are governed by applicable statutory requirements. ABC Public Professional Tax Professional Tax deductions are applied according to state regulations. The deduction amount may vary based on employee location. Income Tax (TDS) Tax Deducted at Source (TDS) is calculated based on: • Declared investments • Tax regime selected by employee • Applicable income tax regulations Employees are responsible for submitting tax declarations before the announced deadline. 6. Overtime Compensation Eligible employees may receive overtime compensation. Overtime is calculated at: 1.5 × standard hourly rate Overtime must receive prior managerial approval. 7. Variable Pay and Incentives Variable compensation may be awarded based on: • Individual performance • Team performance • Business targets • Organizational goals Payment schedules are communicated separately by HR. 8. Reimbursements ABC Public Employees may claim approved reimbursements for: • Business travel • Internet expenses • Mobile expenses • Training expenses Claims must be submitted through the employee portal with supporting documentation. Approved reimbursements are processed in the subsequent payroll cycle. 9. Payslips Payslips are generated monthly. Employees can access payslips through the Employee Self-Service Portal. Payslips include: • Earnings • Deductions • Tax details • Net Pay • Employer Contributions Payslips are retained for 24 months. 10. Bank Account Details Employees are responsible for maintaining accurate banking information. Changes to bank account information must be submitted at least five business days before payroll processing. The organization is not responsible for payment delays caused by incorrect banking information. 11. Payroll Discrepancies Employees should report payroll discrepancies within: ABC Public 7 business days of salary credit. Examples include: • Incorrect salary amount • Missing reimbursement • Incorrect tax deduction • Missing bonus payment Payroll Operations will investigate and resolve valid issues within 10 business days. 12. Bonus Policy Annual bonuses are generally paid during: March Payroll Cycle Bonus eligibility depends on: • Performance rating • Active employment status • Company performance Bonus payouts are not guaranteed unless specified in an employment contract. 13. Confidentiality Payroll information is confidential. Employees must not: • Share salary data of other employees • Access payroll records without authorization • Disclose confidential compensation information Policy violations may lead to disciplinary action. 14. Frequently Asked Questions Q: When is salary credited? ABC Public Answer: Salary is credited on the last working day of each month. Q: How do I download my payslip? Answer: Log in to the Employee Self-Service Portal and select Payroll → Payslips. Q: How is PF calculated? Answer: PF employee contribution is 12% of Basic Salary. Q: When is annual bonus paid? Answer: Eligible bonuses are processed in the March payroll cycle. Q: Who should I contact for payroll issues? Answer: Contact Payroll Operations through the HR Service Desk. ABC Public
